mes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Bad Bunny", "streams": 34855, "best_position": 33}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": 28025, "best_position": 14}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": 15107, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "Mac Miller", "streams": 14754, "best_position": 20}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Toliver", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Eminem", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "metal": {"genre": "metal", "country_code": "ch", "country_name": "Switzerland", "summary": "A metal is a material that exhibits a lustrous appearance when polished or fractured and conducts electricity and heat relatively efficiently. These properties are associated with the presence of electrons at the Fermi level. Metals are typically ductile, allowing them to be drawn into wires, and malleable, enabling them to be shaped by hammering or pressing.\n\nA metal may be a chemical element, such as iron, an alloy such as stainless steel, or a molecular compound such as polymeric sulfur nitride.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": 33368, "best_position": 35}, {"artist": "Bring Me the Horizon", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Metallica", "streams"